      },
      "against": [
        "over"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "end": {
    "over": {
      "when": {
        "calc": "deal > deals"
      },
      "rank_by": "you.score",
      "text": "Winner: {result}. Final scores: Seat 1 {players[0].score}, Seat 2 {players[1].score}, Seat 3 {players[2].score}."
    }
  },
  "limits": {
    "rounds": 36,
    "rounds_max": 40,
    "actions_max": 2000,
    "deadline_s": 120
  },
  "rules": "CARDS. There are {num_cards} cards: four suits, Hearts (H), Bells (B), Leaves (L) and Acorns (A), each with three ranks, Ace (A), Ten (10) and King (K). A card is written rank then suit, for example AH, 10L, KB. Rank order within a suit is A > 10 > K. Card points: each Ace {ace_points}, each Ten {ten_points}, each King {king_points}. Whoever wins the 4th (last) trick of a deal gets {last_trick_bonus} more. The total per deal is {points_per_deal}.\n\nSTRUCTURE. The match is {deals} deals of {tricks_per_deal} tricks each ({total_rounds} rounds). The eldest hand of deal d is seat ((d-1) mod 3)+1, so seats 1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3. Every player starts with score {initial_score}. At the start of each deal the 12 cards are shuffled and each player gets {cards_per_hand}; declarer points, defender points and the multiplier are reset to 0, 0 and {initial_multiplier}.\n\nBID (trick 1, secret, simultaneous). Each player answers PASS or 'N S', where N is 50, 60, 70, 80 or 90 and S is H, B, L or A. The eldest may not pass (PASS or an invalid answer from the eldest counts as '50 A'); an invalid answer from anyone else counts as PASS. The highest N becomes the declarer, with contract N and trump S. On a tie, the tied player first in seat order starting from the eldest wins. The other two are defenders. Base stake = N/{stake_divisor} - {stake_offset} (50 gives 1, 60 gives 2, 70 gives 3, 80 gives 4, 90 gives 5). The declarer leads trick 1. All bids, the declarer, the contract and the trump are announced.\n\nFLEK (trick 2, simultaneous). Each defender answers FLEK or NO, and the declarer answers RE or NO; invalid answers count as NO. If at least one defender said FLEK, the multiplier is multiplied by {flek_factor}; if no defender said FLEK, it stays as it is. If, in addition to a FLEK, the declarer said RE, it is multiplied by {re_factor} again; RE without any FLEK has no effect. All answers and the multiplier are announced.\n\nPLAY. The leader plays any card from their hand; if a named card is not held, their lowest card is played instead. Then the next seat clockwise plays, then the one after. A following player must play a card of the led suit; if they have none, a trump; if they have neither, any card. An illegal or unheld card is replaced by the lowest held led-suit card, else the lowest held trump, else the lowest held card. A trump beats any non-trump; otherwise the highest card of the led suit wins; cards of other suits never win. The trick's points go to the declarer if the declarer won it, otherwise to the defenders, and the winner leads the next trick.\n\nSETTLEMENT (after trick 4). Stake = base stake x multiplier x ({hearts_factor} if trump is Hearts, else 1). If the declarer's points are at least the contract, the declarer gains {declarer_win_factor} x stake and each defender loses stake. Otherwise the declarer loses {declarer_loss_factor} x stake and each defender gains stake.\n\nEND. After deal {deals}, the highest score wins; players tied at the top share the win. There is no discussion."
}
